legacy/docs/spec/statements.md:70:### STMT-4. Evaluation is left to right, assignment evaluates its value first
legacy/docs/spec/statements.md:72:**STMT-4@2.** Subexpressions are evaluated left to right in source order, each completely before the next begins (a call's receiver, then its arguments; a binary operator's left operand, then its right, with `&&` and `||` short-circuiting; literal elements and fields in the order written; a base before its index), except that an assignment evaluates its right-hand side before its destination's subexpressions.
legacy/docs/spec/statements.md:83:**Rationale.** Evaluation remains left to right except that assignment computes its value before its destination; OD53 removes the functional-update evaluation case.
legacy/docs/spec/statements.md:142:### STMT-5. No exit inside an operand
legacy/docs/spec/statements.md:144:**STMT-5@2.** `return`, `break` and `continue` do not occur inside a call argument or receiver, a struct, enum or array literal element, or an operator operand, unless a `break` or `continue` belongs to a loop entered inside that operand.
