legacy/docs/spec/pipeline.md:387:### PASS-10. After Emit: checked operations stay checked, executables have an entry point
legacy/docs/spec/pipeline.md:389:**PASS-10@1.** Every checked operation is emitted through a named helper or a named proven elision and never as a raw wrapping or undefined LLVM operation, and an executable build without an entry point is refused with a `link` diagnostic before the system linker runs.
legacy/docs/spec/arithmetic.md:107:**ARITH-3@1.** `+`, `-`, `*`, unary `-`, `/` and `%` on integers abort when the mathematical result is not representable in the operand type, when the divisor is zero and for `MIN / -1` and `MIN % -1`, and a shift aborts when its count is negative or at least the operand's width and otherwise discards the bits shifted out.
legacy/docs/spec/arithmetic.md:555:**ARITH-11@2.** A named conversion from an integer to a float, or from `f64` to `f32`, rounds to the nearest representable value with ties to even, and each float-to-integer rounding operation (`trunc`, `round`, `floor`, `ceil`) rounds as named and returns the resulting integer when representable, or an error as `try_convert` for NaN, infinities and results outside the target integer range.
