legacy/docs/spec/patterns.md:486:### PAT-10. Irrefutable enum destructuring matches the rest of its block
legacy/docs/spec/patterns.md:488:**PAT-10@2.** An irrefutable enum destructuring `let P = e;` means a one-arm `match` over the rest of its block, with binders visible only there, while a refutable pattern or `let ... else` is refused.
