legacy/docs/spec/patterns.md:509:**PAT-11@2.** An irrefutable destructuring `let mut P = e` declares every binder of `P` mutable, and no destructuring `let` has an `else` block.
legacy/docs/spec/patterns.md:520:**Rationale.** One `mut` applies to each binder; OD52 removes the refutable else form, and immutable binders remain protected by OWN-10.
