docs/decisions.md:1130:| OD15 | <a id="od15"></a>G10: whole-owner freezing under a shared borrow stays. G19: no pass assumes `&mut` exclusivity, and the operational loan rules are defined now | T-G10 (keep the freeze) and T-G19 (the policy sentence) | exit 2i (the G10 decision record), so every deliverable; R-0496, R-0505 | decided 2026-10-29 by the owner. (a) Whole-owner freezing: a live borrow of any part of a value freezes the whole owner, and loans are keyed by the root binding (REF-11 as in the current compiler); this tightens OD2's part 2: at a call, two arguments that borrow the same root conflict whenever one is exclusive, even disjoint fields (`h(&mut a.f, &mut a.g)` is refused, as in the current compiler); OD1's "keyed by the root variable" stands. (b) The strict option: the language guarantees `&mut` exclusivity, which the checker enforces (OD2, OD15a), and no compiler pass or optimization may assume or exploit it until the checker's guarantee is proven in Lean (R-0499 with the Core semantics R-0496); until then the operational loan rules are defined now, G19 included: a pointer or alias derived from a loan is valid only while that loan lives. Now REF-11@3 (partial, bug 319, which OD23 adds) and REF-14 (pending, R-0496) **Canonical current root-based exclusivity subject: REF-11 (including OD23’s re-lent case); OD2 and OD23 refer here rather than defining separate variants.** |
