ROADMAP.md:375:| R-0508 | The end-to-end theorem: maximal-behaviour refinement, frontend correspondence, resource adequacy, image transport | stated in Lean with its holes; proved progressively per slice; every target behaviour theorem has the [target-theorem shape](#target-theorem-shape); the concrete slice-0 theorem is stated and composed before B0 closes, retaining the maximal-behaviour, resource, observation and image-transport obligations | R-0496, R-0502 |
ROADMAP.md:404:| R-0593 | The diagnostic and facts records, their frozen, versioned JSON schema, goldens and the parser's diagnostics from the first front-end output ([diagnostics decision](docs/decisions.md#decided-project-diagnostics-2026-11-06), [early decision](docs/decisions.md#decided-2026-11-07-early-evidence)) | every slice-0 refusal is one typed record rendered as human text and JSON lines (`--format=human|json`), with rule IDs from the Lean rule name and that rule's own revision (R-0603); the diagnostics and facts JSON schema is frozen and versioned from the first front-end output, and golden tests cover it and both diagnostic renderings; the LL(1) parser fills its expected-token set from the grammar data; B0's classified refusal controls use the records; Home: spec (the diagnostics and facts types are the schema source). Gate: the JSON schema generated from the Lean types, with goldens ([tracking](docs/decisions.md#decided-2026-11-07-tracking)) | R-0592, R-0575 |
