- Codex C6 columns — accepted: [runtime](../docs/decisions.md#decided-project-runtime-2026-11-06) fixes 1-based columns only; question 10 isolates byte/tab counting.
- Codex C6 concurrency — accepted: slice 28 remains undecided; require preservation of complete single-thread/no-interference runs, not deletion of synchronization from interfering runs.
- Codex C7 — accepted: [INFOFLOW](../docs/archive/crucial-2026-11-06/INFOFLOW.md) specifies delimited release; C7 defines policy authorization, ordered site/value equality and separate NI/CT obligations, including allocation sizes and loop counts.
- Codex C8 — accepted: retain Q9.9 adequacy and fuel distinctions; add explicit choices and Core IR as requested by agy.
- Codex C9 — accepted: retain independent judgments, evidence and erasure under Q9.10–Q9.13; separate registry extension approval.
- Codex C10 — accepted: retain frame/ABI contracts under Q8.5–Q8.6 and P18; repair the earlier-memory wording consistently with C4.
- Codex S3 certificates — accepted: [compiler-execution trust](../docs/decisions.md#decided-project-long-term-2026-11-06) explicitly requires kernel-checked exact-input→BIR certificates and backend-input binding, not merely universal pass proofs.
- Codex S3 maximal behavior — accepted: Q9.9 explicitly calls for maximal behaviors; each edge now excludes infinite silent target stuttering as well as preserving observations.
- Codex register OD126 — accepted: [OD126](../docs/decisions.md#od126) includes the existing profile; target generalization preserves its constants while enum layout is separately answerable.
