- Codex register remaining rows — accepted: retain the substance of Q3.5/Q3.7/Q3.9/Q1.7/TYPE-19/FFI-7/FFI-10/Q7.10/Q9.7 proposals, split by independent change; no revision is enacted.
- Codex DEC1 — accepted: draft 2 is a corrected proposal, not a claim that contracts or proofs are complete.
- Codex DEC2 — accepted: independent target, usize, enum, release-context and registry questions replace blanket register approval.
- Codex DEC3 — accepted: add tagged-now/future-owner-approval option; recommend it because the extensible representation laws do not require a permanent niche inventory.
- Codex DEC4 — accepted: questions 8 and 17 separate image milestone from qualification, matching distinct Q8.1/pipeline obligations.
- Codex unflagged findings — accepted: option-b provenance, columns, TrapKind and owning Text are addressed individually above; none is attributed to an invented decided row.

- Kimi S1 — accepted: retain the extensible interface boundary, qualified by A2i’s proved/tested scope and the supplied owner answer.
- Kimi C1 — partly accepted: core sequencing/cleanup matches Q2/Q9; agreement does not justify the unrecorded collection orders, now deferred in question 13.
- Kimi C2 — accepted: [TYPE-20](../legacy/docs/spec/types.md#TYPE-20) makes char one byte with every-u8 round trip; [OD137](../docs/decisions.md#od137) restricts literals, not stored code units.
- Kimi C3 — partly accepted: layout laws are useful, but OD126’s i32 tags and TYPE-3 owning Text prevent treating all draft-1 representations as decided; split enum question and repair Text.
- Kimi C4 — accepted: Q3.7’s row note explicitly permits zero-byte access with only alignment and non-null address; distinguish initialization for reads from write permission and retain byte-valued char.
- Kimi C5 — partly accepted: retain decided ownership/authority; Q7.10 contains no Entropy instance, so its exact shape cannot be frozen by agreement.
- Kimi C6 — partly accepted: runtime format and environment distinctions stand, but column counting and trap strings are new; isolate them and defer concurrency details.
