- Kimi unflagged findings — accepted: remove Unicode-scalar char and zero-byte access tightening rather than proposing revisions to TYPE-20/Q3.7.

- agy citation-verification request — accepted: checked the pipeline/Core rows and relevant OD/spec rules; Q7.10 confirms exits 125/134, Q3.9 reconstruction, Q8.5–Q8.6 retention, and Q9.14/A2i proof obligations; no authority is inferred from agy’s repo-blind review.
- agy S1 — partly accepted: retain extensible foundation scope but make the dated owner answer and A2i restriction explicit.
- agy C1 — accepted: Q9.6 uses checked destructor bodies; no cited row establishes those array/OrderedMap orders, so question 13 defers them.
- agy C2 — partly accepted: isolate checked-conversion error type and UTF-8 mapping; reject the implication that checked error values must be merged into TrapKind, since Q6.7 distinguishes them.
- agy C3 — accepted: Q3.7/raw operations and OD126/FFI-7 layout queries contradict blanket layout independence; use a read-only interface and separate enum question.
