- agy C9 struct invariants — partly accepted: defer source implementation to slice 17, but [SPARK](../docs/decisions.md#decided-project-spark-2026-11-06) already decides exposure rules and requires their spec definition before freeze; do not defer that definition.
- agy C9 ensures timing — rejected: Q9.11, [OD144](../docs/decisions.md#od144) and CON-3 explicitly decide post-cleanup observation; retain it rather than invent a new timing question.
- agy C10 — accepted: Memory CFG is the explicit representation/ABI lowering boundary, not the first semantic existence of raw bytes or layout queries.
- agy S3 — accepted: specify hybrid Core reference execution, matched profile/choices and representation simulations; this makes layout/raw observations comparable with LLVM and LCB.
- agy register OD126 — accepted: separate target abstraction from enum tag sizing and payload layout.
- agy register FFI-7 — accepted: enum layout and sizeof/alignof return-type changes are independently answerable.
- agy register Q7.10 — accepted: remove the C5/nullary-Entropy contradiction and defer a complete instance consistently.
- agy DEC1 — accepted: repair state/evaluator contradictions and expose undecided rules before requesting a freeze.
- agy DEC2 — accepted: enum layout and Entropy instance are no longer hidden in blanket register approval.
- agy DEC3 — partly accepted: include permanent no-niches option (c), but recommend tagged-now option (b); no decided row makes a permanent prohibition necessary for readable code or representation proofs.
- agy DEC4 — partly accepted: accept independent complete-observation qualification; reject automatic advancement to 0.1 because Q8.1 and ROADMAP retain a later conditional-native closure milestone requiring a separate owner answer.
- agy unflagged list — partly accepted: separately expose trap strings, conversion error, UTF-8 mapping, enum layout, destruction and Entropy; struct exposure and post-cleanup ensures are already decided, so only implementation scheduling remains open.
